WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.674
Advanced grouping introduces an important NULL
question Subtotal

00:00:05.687 --> 00:00:09.647
and grand-total rows often show NULL in grouping
columns because that dimension

00:00:09.674 --> 00:00:14.005
has been rolled up But source data can also contain
genuine NULL

00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:21.163
values GROUPING helps us distinguish those two
situations A

00:00:21.177 --> 00:00:25.005
grouping code tells us which expressions are
participating in the current row

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:30.195
and which have been summarized away The exact code
is less important

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:33.721
than the principle do not label every NULL with
COALESCE before you

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:38.790
know why it is NULL In a production report using
GROUPING can

00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:43.133
help you label rows accurately as detail subtotal or
grand total without

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:45.896
confusing structural placeholders with missing data
